<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Ahmsa agrees to workers' pay hike.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Ahmsa agrees to workers' pay hike.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican steel company Altos Hornos SA (Ahmsa) has avoided a looming strike threat by agreeing to grant an 18 percent wage hike to its workers at its steel plant number one, officials said.</p>
<p>The Labor Ministry said in a statement the pay hike was effective immediately and would benefit 5,011 workers. It added that the agreement avoided a strike that had been called by Ahmsa workers for March 10.</p>
<p>((--David Luhnow, Mexico City newsroom 525 728-9565))</p>
